{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cea07f808ff55270","type":"text","text":"Anselm- the last human left ","x":-403,"y":59,"width":283,"height":101},
		{"id":"ef153808d33a5d97","type":"text","text":"Large intellect and vast philosophical and analytical knowledge cuz all he does is read and write. However he misunderstand some philosophical ideas and due to his unique isolation he has nobody to tell him has wrong or produce contradictory evidence. Strict believer in nihilism absurdism  ","x":-500,"y":300,"width":283,"height":300},
		{"id":"6c15e142ed81dc53","type":"text","text":"Refuses to indulge because it goes against his ideas and he is very stubborn ","x":-358,"y":-220,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"b9b4825399706346","type":"text","text":"Believes that life is a gift and that it should be lived subjectively and actively no matter what. Furthermore he believes that all life has unique purpose and meaning that must be defined by the person who lives it and that by not living life the Syncors posses no meaning or purpose and therefore have no value. He views them with both pity and disdain. He pity's their lack of life and holds disdain for them since they represent contradicting ideas","x":145,"y":-340,"width":495,"height":360},
		{"id":"cd1c9f705658d9eb","type":"text","text":"He believes he has an inherent meaning, purpose, and value through 3 key things ","x":-975,"y":6,"width":250,"height":154},
		{"id":"d089e9a8a3a29f2c","type":"text","text":"### Purpose \nHe writes and reads; indulging in knowledge and intellect, contributing to the vastness of literary works defining his [[Purpose]]. what he writes, however, is cliche and essentially just other ideas restated. ","x":-1225,"y":-550,"width":250,"height":420},
		{"id":"25b1211f692622e3","type":"text","text":"His subconscious mind, however, understands that he has no defensible meaning or purpose which is why has so depressed and cynical. He only becomes happy when he starts to kill the Syncors and find actual meaning and purpose in killing the Syncors and eventually attempting to kill the Elites. \n","x":-798,"y":-640,"width":395,"height":368},
		{"id":"1d7191fe64727b7a","type":"text","text":"He hates the elite because they are indifferent and quite insular. They lack the human condition  and they have exhausted their meaning and purpose. Essentially he views them the same as the Syncors. Devoid of humanity and lacking of meaning or purpose as they spend all their time engulfed in meaningless purposeless life as they sit atop Abadon, a utopia with every need catered to, doing nothing just like the Syncors. Or so he thinks. He also has a special hate for them because they created the Syncors whom he hates. . \nHe lives in his awful apartment because he finds it oddly comforting AND he spites luxury because it strips meaning. ","x":98,"y":280,"width":455,"height":360},
		{"id":"bc2e79d63c376e39","type":"text","text":"Examines the question: What happens when people refuse to conform, opting instead to delve into individuality and isolation? what happens when people are left to their own devices with nobody to correct them and teach them? explores themes of isolation, conformity, delusion, meaning, purpose, intellect. ","x":125,"y":-640,"width":401,"height":220},
		{"id":"be19852aeb320685","type":"text","text":"### Value \nHe refuses to conform to society; His refusal to conform is his validation. By refusing to conform he sees himself as a unique intellect and therefore of [[Value]] to the human race ","x":-1300,"y":-42,"width":250,"height":250},
		{"id":"e16d7e1b04a2bf74","type":"text","text":"### Meaning \nHe believes he has meaning through his value and purpose. They prove his existence matters. Furthermore, isolation has given way to delusions of sorts where he believes hes meant for greatness.  [[Meaning]]","x":-1225,"y":280,"width":250,"height":294},
		{"id":"1bb0d8e4276214ed","type":"text","text":"### The Snap\n\nWhat causes Anselm to finally snap and begin killing the Syncors is when one day hes late to work. on his way, however, he notices something off, one of the Syncors is smiling. A faint smile but still a smile. For a split second hes filled with contempt because a body devoid of value experienced joy when he himself is woefully depressed. He catches himself envying a thing he's called worthless. He can't handle the idea that an inferior being can experience things he himself cannot due to his own hubris. He kills the Syncor, and then feels joy.  Killing the Syncor not only validated himself as a superior being of intellect and life but also bestows him with a purpose ","x":-355,"y":-1080,"width":500,"height":380},
		{"id":"d53a1f55e8636962","x":933,"y":116,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"[[Me]]"}
	],
